Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:50:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 117/143] pci: sunxi: correct the SII IRQ number in the irqmask
 comment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The comment claimed the SII line is GIC SPI 117.  The device tree
wires "sii" to GIC_SPI 106 (sun55i-a523.dtsi), and the T527 user
manual interrupt source table agrees: source 138 "PCIE_SII", i.e.
SPI 138 - 32 = 106.  The substance of the comment (level-triggered
line, link bits left masked at their power-on default) is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
index a9c87429d..591000dc3 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sunxi_pcie_plat_ltssm_disable);
 static void sunxi_pcie_plat_set_irqmask(struct sunxi_pcie *pci)
 {
 	/*
-	 * The SII interrupt line is level-triggered (GIC SPI 117,
+	 * The SII interrupt line is level-triggered (GIC SPI 106,
 	 * IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH, see sun55i-a523.dtsi) and the SII_INT_1 link
 	 * bits (0xE0C bits 0/1, SMLH/RDLH_LINK_UP) read back as live level
 	 * status per the T527 user manual v0.92 §8.13.5.35.  The driver does
